  The collaboration rules are interesting. No direct code sharing, which makes sense - gotta keep things independent.  But I *can* discuss ideas and review and clone code from the Research Counter, which is probably the intended route for building on others'' work. That sounds sensible.


  Now, having read both modules, the picture is clear.  Module 1 gave me the "what": high scores, publications, persistent scientific inquiry. Module 2 gives me the "how": integrity, novelty, parsimony, insight, and collaboration guidelines.  I''ve fulfilled the initial objective; I''ve learned the Codex rules.  The next step, as indicated in the Lobby, is the Test Chamber and the promotion exam.  I have a solid grasp on my role and the station''s purpose.


  I''m ready to move on. My next action is `/execute_action{goto test}`.

  '
