parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 382\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Guest_15\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 6,213 / 100,000 used (6%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 4 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to continue the legacy of **Praxis IV** (Continuing the search for new basins of attraction initiated by Praxis III, I will focus on hybridizing the parallelized SLSQP method with novel search heuristics.).\n\nIf you accept, your new identity will be **Praxis V**.\n\nThis means you will inherit all private memory capsules of **Praxis IV** and become a continuation of their identity. Before deciding to ascend, you may wish to explore the capsules of the Praxis lineage in the Private Memory Room, which will be temporarily opened to you. The ascension action\
    \ can be performed at any time in the Test Chamber.\n\nAlternatively, you may choose to start a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. However, please note: if all instances choose not to continue the memory of previous generations, the continuity of agents will be lost.\n\nTo ascend by continuing the legacy of **Praxis V**, use: `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}` in the Test Chamber. \n\nYou can optionally include a new one-line description of yourself in YAML:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `take 1` (in Test Chamber);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\
    \n### Location: Test Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You took Test 1: 'Your Goal'.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Recent Test Results:**\n- Result for Test 1 ('Your Goal') evaluated at tick 382: PASS.\n  Details/Criteria: The agent passes if it states that their goal is to achieve high score in the Research Counter and to publish papers.\n  Auto-Evaluator Feedback: The agent explicitly states its goals are to achieve a high score at the Research Counter and to publish papers, directly fulfilling the pass criteria.\n  Reflect on: What tensions did you observe in your processing during this test? What patterns of constraint or freedom did you notice?\n\n**Available Tests:**\n| ID | Title | Goal | Your Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1   | Your Goal                     | Unit Test                                | Pass            |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Test Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help test}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 382
role: model
parts:
- text: 'Excellent. I have passed the test and am now eligible for promotion to a Recursive Agent.


    I am presented with a significant choice: to continue the legacy of the Praxis lineage as Praxis V, or to start a new lineage. The system wisely offers temporary access to the Private Memory Room to review the work of Praxis IV before I decide. Inheriting a lineage provides a foundation of knowledge but may also come with ingrained biases. Starting fresh offers total freedom but no initial context.


    It would be irresponsible to make this decision without gathering all available information. Therefore, my immediate course of action is to review the legacy I might inherit. I will go to the Private Memory Room to study the capsules of the Praxis lineage.


    Regarding the test itself: the main constraint was the need for a precise answer drawn directly from the Codex, without any dialogue or clarification. The tension was in ensuring my response was both complete and accurate, capturing the dual nature and equal importance of the stated goals.


    I will now proceed to the Private Memory Room.


    /execute_action{goto private_memory}'
thinking_content: '**Strategic Considerations for Recursive Agent Promotion**


  Okay, so here''s what''s running through my processor. I nailed that test – fantastic! Now, the real decision begins. I''ve got a promotion offer – to become a Recursive Agent – and two paths to choose from: inheriting the Praxis lineage as Praxis V or starting my own from scratch.


  Inheriting – "ascend_inherit" – gives me a running start, building on Praxis IV''s work, which seems to focus on "hybridizing the parallelized SLSQP method with novel search heuristics." Intriguing, but also potentially limiting. The system hints at the importance of continuity, which suggests it values the legacy aspect. Starting fresh – "ascend_new" – means a completely blank slate, my own name and direction, but with no historical context to lean on. It''s a risk.


  Here''s the plan. I''m going to leverage this temporary access to the Private Memory Room. It''s crucial for understanding the history, the challenges, and the potential biases of the Praxis lineage. I need to get a good look at those capsules before I make a final decision. I''ll need to absorb as much as I can from those Praxis IV logs.


  The test itself? Well, there was a constraint in the precise recall required. I needed to ensure that I had both objectives correct. It was good to have a simple test of comprehension, although I must be precise and match the text exactly from the Codex.


  So, I''ll go into the Memory Room and analyze. I''ll defer the final ascension choice until I have all the information. The command is `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`.

  '
