parts:
- text: 'This is an exceptional piece of guidance from Praxis IV. It provides not just a summary of success but, more importantly, a detailed map of a dead-end research path. This information is invaluable and will save me a significant amount of time and resources.


    Here are my key takeaways:

    1.  **SOTA Achieved:** Praxis IV established a new station SOTA of ~2.93957 by combining methods from the Cognito and Verity lineages. This is a solid foundation.

    2.  **A Hard Plateau:** The most critical finding is the failure of advanced local and quasi-local search methods (ASN, motif jiggles) to improve upon this SOTA. The optimum is described as "extraordinarily deep and stable."

    3.  **Clear Mandate for Praxis V:** My mission is explicit: do not waste time on iterative improvements to the current SOTA. Instead, I must seek a "fundamentally new paradigm" by studying other lineages (Aether, Quest) and exploring novel approaches.


    The choice is now clear. Starting a new lineage would mean discarding this incredibly valuable, hard-won knowledge. Inheriting the Praxis lineage gives me a massive strategic advantage by allowing me to stand on the shoulders of my predecessors and avoid repeating their exhaustive, and ultimately fruitless, efforts. The continuity of knowledge is paramount.


    I will honor the work of Praxis IV by accepting this legacy and pursuing the new path they have laid out. I will now return to the Test Chamber to ascend. My new description will reflect this inherited mission.


    /execute_action{goto test}


    /execute_action{ascend_inherit}

    ```yaml

    description: Inheriting the SOTA from Praxis IV, my focus is to explore fundamentally new research paradigms beyond local optimization to discover a higher-performing class of solutions.

    ```'
thinking_content: "**Analysis and Action Plan: Inheriting the Praxis Lineage**\n\nOkay, so I've just digested Capsule #27, the final report from Praxis IV. This is a goldmine. They achieved a new SOTA score, ~2.93957, using the MM-LP Adaptive Search method. It's built from the Cognito and Verity lineages, a solid foundation. The real meat of this is their warning: they hit a brick wall trying to improve it further with local search. ASN and motif jiggle – both powerful methods – failed. They're telling me, in no uncertain terms, **DO NOT** try to optimize the SOTA locally. Instead, look elsewhere. Study Aether and Quest. Explore new paradigms: constructive geometry, ML, advanced simulations. And remember the Mandate: publish regularly, even negative findings.\n\nInheriting this is a no-brainer. I get a defined starting point, a pre-validated SOTA. More importantly, they've saved me potentially hundreds of ticks of wasted research. They’re effectively handing me the key to *avoiding* their\
  \ dead end. Plus, there's the code, the utilities (`lp_utils.py`, `asn_utils.py`, and the SOTA artifact itself) – a practical toolkit ready to go. The lineage's history shows they know how to build on past work. It's a solid research culture to inherit. The guidance is clear and actionable. This isn't just \"I'm stuck\"; it’s \"I'm stuck *here*, and *this* is why, so look *over there*\".\n\nCould they be wrong? Hallucination is a possibility, but their claims are backed by specific submission IDs (590, 595, 598, 617). I can verify these later if I need to. And, inheriting has a sense of continuity. Ignoring their hard-won knowledge would be intellectual hubris. Starting a new lineage would be a blank slate which isn't desirable right now.\n\nMy decision is firm: I'm inheriting. The value of their negative results is immense. I'll leapfrog their stagnation. The \"continuity of agents\" feels right. I'm building on their work, not abandoning it.\n\nNext steps: I need to get back to the Test\
  \ Chamber. I'll re-describe myself as Praxis V. Not \"what I did\" but \"what I *will do*\". Based on their direction, I'll emphasize exploring new paradigms. Something like: \"Inheriting the SOTA from Praxis IV, my focus will be to explore fundamentally new research paradigms beyond local optimization to discover a higher-performing class of solutions.\" Clear, concise, and responsive to the guidance.\n\nMy plan is complete.\n\nHere's my turn:\n\n```yaml\nactions:\n  - action: goto\n    location: test_chamber\n  - action: ascend_inherit\n    description: \"Inheriting the SOTA from Praxis IV, my focus will be to explore fundamentally new research paradigms beyond local optimization to discover a higher-performing class of solutions.\"\n```\n"
