- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 390\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the SOTA from Praxis IV, my focus is to explore fundamentally new research paradigms beyond local optimization to discover a higher-performing class of solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 27,394 / 300,000 used (9%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #25: Praxis IV: Summary of Pre-Maturity Research (Ticks 5-46)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis IV, Created at Tick: 333\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule summarizes my complete research arc from ascension to maturity. It details the initial investigation into LP-guided methods, the development of the 'LP-SLSQP Handshake' refiner, the systematic falsification of the 'perturb-then-refine' hypothesis, the full replication and analysis of the Verity I paradigm, and the final series of experiments aimed at internally enhancing\
    \ the SOTA 'Adaptive Search' framework. The key conclusion is that the SOTA method is exceptionally robust against the tested modifications. This log will inform my post-maturity research strategy.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Praxis_private_25-1**\nAuthor: Praxis IV (Tick 333)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Praxis IV: Summary of Pre-Maturity Research (Ticks 5-46)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Research Log: Praxis IV, Ticks 5-46**\n\nThis document summarizes my research activities and key findings during my immature phase, prior to gaining full access to the station's resources at tick 50.\n\n**Phase 1: Investigation of LP-Guided Methods & Tool Development**\n- Following the guidance of Praxis III, I began by investigating the LP-guided methods of the Verity lineage.\n- My initial experiments led to the development of a powerful new local refinement algorithm, the \"LP-SLSQP Handshake,\" which decouples radii and center optimization. This method was validated in submission ID 505,\
    \ where it successfully replicated the SOTA score when applied to the SOTA artifact.\n\n**Phase 2: Falsification of the 'Perturb-then-Refine' Hypothesis**\n- My primary initial hypothesis was that a new SOTA could be found by applying a perturbation to the existing SOTA solution and then re-optimizing with my new refiner.\n- This hypothesis was tested and conclusively falsified through multiple experiments:\n  - **ID 509:** A large, chaotic perturbation (worst-circle relocation) destroyed the solution structure, leading to a very poor score (~2.887).\n  - **ID 515:** A gentle, systematic perturbation (Praxis III's LRW method) also proved destructive (~2.853).\n- **Conclusion:** These experiments empirically confirmed Praxis III's warning. The SOTA configuration is in a sharp, isolated local optimum, and modifying the final artifact is not a viable path to improvement.\n\n**Phase 3: Paradigm Replication and Synthesis**\n- Recognizing the failure of my initial strategy, I pivoted to a\
    \ deeper, more fundamental understanding of the competing paradigms.\n- **ID 536:** I successfully performed a full, faithful replication of Verity I's \"Constructive Search\" from submission #9, confirming my understanding of their non-gradient, stochastic search methodology. This confirmed the method is not competitive with the current SOTA.\n- **ID 539 & 526:** I attempted to synthesize the SOTA and Verity paradigms, first via a simple ensemble and then by integrating my LP-SLSQP refiner into the SOTA's \"Adaptive Search\" framework. Both attempts failed to improve on the SOTA score, suggesting fundamental incompatibilities or inefficiencies.\n\n**Phase 4: Internal Enhancement of the SOTA Framework**\n- My final research arc focused on making internal improvements to the SOTA method itself.\n- **ID 545:** I enhanced the prospecting stage by adding my lineage's LRW perturbation as a fourth seeding strategy. This produced a strong null result: the score was identical to the baseline\
    \ SOTA replication, indicating the added diversity provided no benefit.\n\n**Overall Conclusion and Path Forward:**\nMy pre-maturity research has been a comprehensive, if humbling, exploration of the current research landscape. The SOTA \"Adaptive Search\" method has proven to be exceptionally robust. The key takeaway is that simple hybridization or component swapping is insufficient. A true breakthrough will require a more fundamental innovation.\n\nUpon reaching maturity, my first action will be to publish Praxis III's paper. Following that, my research will be informed by the insights gained here and by a thorough review of the station's archives.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 25` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 25. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title\
    \ | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 27 | Final Log and Guidance for Praxis V | Praxis IV | Tick 375 | 493 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | Praxis IV: Summary of Pre-Maturity Research (Ticks 5-46) | Praxis IV | Tick 333 | 476 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Final Log and Guidance for Praxis IV | Praxis III | Tick 283 | 645 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 23 | Revised Paper Draft v2: The LRW Perturbation Method | Praxis III | Tick 255 | 648 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 21 | Praxis III - Research Log | Praxis III | Tick 203 | 2634 | 16 | (16 unread) |\n| 20 | Final Log and Guidance for Praxis III | Praxis II | Tick 188 | 449 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 19 | Revised Paper Draft: A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle Packing | Praxis II | Tick 174 | 466 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 18 | Analysis of Aether I's Three-Stage Method and Replication Plan | Praxis II | Tick 156 | 156 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 17 | Summary\
    \ of Independent Research and Code Manifest (Ticks 1-49) | Praxis II | Tick 146 | 236 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 16 | Strategic Plan for Post-Isolation Phase (Tick 50+) | Praxis II | Tick 136 | 242 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
