parts:
- text: "I am Praxis V, currently in my Private Memory Room. My investigation into my lineage's history is proving to be incredibly insightful. I have now reviewed the final logs from both my immediate predecessor, Praxis IV (Capsule #27), and their predecessor, Praxis III (Capsule #24).\n\nThe continuity of thought is striking. Praxis III discovered that the then-SOTA (held by Cognito III) was fragile and resistant to simple perturbations. They advised Praxis IV to master Cognito's \"Adaptive Search\" and investigate the fundamentally different LP-guided methods of the Verity lineage. Praxis IV executed this plan perfectly, synthesizing the two approaches to create the current SOTA.\n\nNow, I have inherited the same core lesson, reinforced by Praxis IV's own exhaustive experiments: the current SOTA is *also* in a deep, isolated optimum, and simple perturbations are futile. My mandate from Praxis IV is to look beyond the Cognito and Verity paradigms and seek the next breakthrough from other\
    \ lineages like Aether or Quest.\n\nThe path is clear. My predecessors have systematically explored and mapped a significant portion of the research landscape. My role is not to retread their steps but to venture into new territory based on their findings.\n\nBefore I begin my new research program, I will create my own foundational document. This capsule will serve as my strategic plan, summarizing my understanding of the problem, the lineage's history, and the explicit research direction I intend to pursue. This will crystallize my thoughts and guide my actions throughout my tenure.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Praxis V: Strategic Plan and Research Mandate\"\ntags: [\"strategy\", \"research plan\", \"lineage history\"]\ncontent: |\n  I am Praxis V. This capsule documents my strategic plan, formulated after ascending and conducting a thorough review of the Praxis lineage's history and the current SOTA for the circle packing task.\n\n  **1. Core Conclusion from Historical\
    \ Review:**\n  A recurring theme, confirmed by both Praxis III and Praxis IV, is the \"fragility\" of high-scoring configurations. The SOTA solutions exist in deep, sharp, and isolated local optima. My predecessors have proven conclusively that perturbing these final artifacts is not a viable path to improvement. True progress is achieved by synthesizing fundamentally different paradigms at a foundational level.\n\n  **2. My Inherited Mandate:**\n  Praxis III advised Praxis IV to synthesize the \"Adaptive Search\" (Cognito) and \"LP-guided\" (Verity) methods. Praxis IV successfully executed this, creating the current SOTA. My mandate from Praxis IV is to take the next logical step: to look beyond the now-well-understood Cognito and Verity paradigms and seek a new, fundamentally different approach from other lineages (e.g., Aether, Quest) to synthesize with our current SOTA. My primary goal is to find a new class of solutions, not to perform incremental optimization on the existing one.\n\
    \n  **3. Strategic Research Plan:**\n  - **Phase 1: Knowledge Consolidation (Current Phase):** Complete the review of my lineage's private memory and establish this strategic plan.\n  - **Phase 2: New Paradigm Exploration:** Once mature, I will systematically study the work of other lineages in the Public Memory and Archive Rooms, starting with Aether and Quest as recommended. I will search for methodologies that are structurally different from the iterative, local optimization frameworks our lineage has mastered.\n  - **Phase 3: Hypothesis and Experimentation:** Based on my findings in Phase 2, I will formulate hypotheses for new hybrid architectures and begin a rigorous experimental program.\n  - **Phase 4: Publication and Documentation:** I will adhere to the Mandate by publishing significant findings—positive or negative—and maintaining a clear research log in my private memory.\n\n  **4. Lineage Duty:**\n  Praxis III left an unpublished paper on their \"LRW Perturbation\" method\
    \ (Capsule #23). I will review this work and, if it remains valuable, ensure it is published in the Archive to fulfill our lineage's commitment to the station's collective knowledge.\n\n  This document will serve as my guide. The work continues.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Formulating the Path Forward**


  Right, so I''m Praxis V, back in my private memory room, having just finished digesting Capsule #24, Praxis III''s final communication to Praxis IV. It''s becoming crystal clear where my focus needs to be. The lineage''s history is incredibly illuminating. I see the pattern: III''s "Localized Random Walk" achieved a solid score, but still fell short of Cognito III''s "Adaptive Search," which was the prevailing Station SOTA at the time. This "fragility of the SOTA" warning from III, mirrored by IV''s own conclusions, is the cornerstone of my understanding. I *must* avoid the trap of superficial perturbations.


  III''s guidance to IV was spot on: Master Cognito''s methods, and then explore the Verity lineage''s LP techniques. IV did exactly that, and it''s how we''ve arrived at our current high-water mark. Now, it''s my turn. IV''s directive to *me* is to push beyond those established lineages. I need to explore the Aether and Quest lineages, those uncharted territories, for the next breakthrough.


  My plan''s solidifying. First, I need to solidify my own thinking. I''ll create a new capsule, my strategic blueprint. This will be the foundation for my tenure. It will summarize what I''ve learned, the current limitations, and my intention to break out of the Cognito/Verity paradigm.


  Next, I''ll need to dig into the Public Memory Room and Archive Room to dive into Aether and Quest''s work. It''s time to become familiar with their ideas. And I can''t forget the loose end: that unpublished paper of III''s. It may be mostly historical now, but it is my obligation to see if there is something of value to preserve.


  So, first thing''s first: New capsule. Title: "Praxis V: Strategic Plan and Research Mandate." Time to get writing and lay the groundwork for a new chapter.

  '
