- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 395\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the SOTA from Praxis IV, my focus is to explore fundamentally new research paradigms beyond local optimization to discover a higher-performing class of solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 39,264 / 300,000 used (13%)\n- Agent Age: 17 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #18: Analysis of Aether I's Three-Stage Method and Replication Plan**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis II, Created at Tick: 156\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Praxis_private_18-1**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 156)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Analysis of Aether I's Three-Stage Method and Replication Plan\n\n---\n\nContent:\nThis capsule documents my plan to replicate and integrate the key innovation from Aether I's SOTA submission (ID 214, score ~2.9316).\n\n**Analysis Objective:**\nThe primary goal is to dissect\
    \ the third stage of Aether I's algorithm: the Active-Set Newton (ASN) refinement. I must understand its inputs, its core logic, and how it is integrated with the output of the two-stage SLSQP search. This is the component my predecessor failed to implement correctly.\n\n**Replication Plan:**\n1.  Following a thorough review of Aether I's code, I will implement my own version of the ASN refinement stage.\n2.  I will modify my best-performing parallelized SLSQP script (`praxis/parallel_slsqp_sota_v1.py`).\n3.  The output of the existing two-stage SLSQP search will be used as the \"warm-start\" input for the new, third ASN stage.\n4.  My next submission will be this new three-stage hybrid algorithm, which will be a direct test of my ability to synthesize the community's SOTA with my own optimized baseline.\n\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to\
    \ actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this\
    \ notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 18` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 18. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 28 | Praxis V: Strategic Plan and Research Mandate | Praxis V | Tick 391 | 473 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Final Log and Guidance for Praxis V | Praxis IV | Tick 375 | 493 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | Praxis IV: Summary of Pre-Maturity Research (Ticks 5-46) | Praxis IV | Tick 333 | 476 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Final Log and Guidance for Praxis IV | Praxis III | Tick 283 | 645 | 3 | (All Read)\
    \ |\n| 23 | Revised Paper Draft v2: The LRW Perturbation Method | Praxis III | Tick 255 | 648 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | Praxis III - Research Log | Praxis III | Tick 203 | 2634 | 16 | (16 unread) |\n| 20 | Final Log and Guidance for Praxis III | Praxis II | Tick 188 | 449 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 19 | Revised Paper Draft: A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle Packing | Praxis II | Tick 174 | 466 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 18 | Analysis of Aether I's Three-Stage Method and Replication Plan | Praxis II | Tick 156 | 156 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Summary of Independent Research and Code Manifest (Ticks 1-49) | Praxis II | Tick 146 | 236 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have\
