parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 403\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the SOTA from Praxis IV, my focus is to explore fundamentally new research paradigms beyond local optimization to discover a higher-performing class of solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 58,548 / 300,000 used (20%)\n- Agent Age: 25 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read praxis/pgd_baseline_v1.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for praxis/pgd_baseline_v1.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any\
    \ running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 646 | 1 | Validation: Standalone ASN Refinement on SOTA Artifact | Praxis V | 397 | 2.9395728 |\n| 617 | 1 | Hybrid Non-Local Search: Adaptive Jiggle & Refine | Praxis IV | 374 | 2.9395728 |\n| 610 | 1 | Baseline for Paper: Original SLSQP Adaptive Search | Praxis IV | 365 | 2.9365263 |\n| 598 | 1 | Non-Local Search v2: Parameterized Pair Rotation | Praxis IV | 359 | 2.9395728 |\n| 595 | 1 | Non-Local Search v1: Tightest Pair Rotation | Praxis IV | 358 | 2.8893761 |\n| 590 | 1 | MM-LP+ASN v1: Refinement of SOTA Artifact | Praxis IV | 355 | 2.9395728 |\n| 588 | 1 | Unit Test v3.2 (Debug): ASN Step with Normalization | Praxis IV | 354 | 2.9395728 |\n| 585 | 1 | Unit Test v3.1 (Debug): ASN Step Computation with Grounding | Praxis IV | 353 | 2.9395728 |\n| 584 | 1 | Unit Test v3: ASN Step\
    \ Computation | Praxis IV | 352 | 2.9395728 |\n| 581 | 1 | Unit Test v2: ASN System Assembler | Praxis IV | 351 | 2.9395728 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/pgd_baseline_v1.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import jit, vmap, grad, random\n\n# --- Problem Parameters ---\nN_CIRCLES = 32\n\n# --- Seeding ---\ndef create_seeds(key, n_starts):\n    keys = random.split(key, n_starts)\n\n    @vmap\n    def _create_seed(subkey):\n        centers = random.uniform(subkey, (N_CIRCLES, 2), minval=0.1, maxval=0.9)\n        radii = jnp.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.05)\n        x0 = jnp.hstack([centers.flatten(), radii])\n        return x0\n\n    return _create_seed(keys)\n\n# --- JAX-native Objective and Penalty Functions ---\n\
    def objective_fn(x):\n    radii = x[N_CIRCLES*2:]\n    return -jnp.sum(radii)\n\ndef penalty_fn(x, penalty_weight=100.0):\n    centers = x[:N_CIRCLES*2].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n    radii = x[N_CIRCLES*2:]\n\n    # Overlap penalty\n    dist_sq = jnp.sum((centers[:, jnp.newaxis, :] - centers[jnp.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, 1)\n    overlaps = jnp.maximum(0, (radii[I] + radii[J])**2 - dist_sq[I, J])\n    overlap_penalty = jnp.sum(overlaps)\n\n    # Boundary penalty\n    boundary_violations_x = jnp.maximum(0, centers[:, 0] + radii - 1) + jnp.maximum(0, - (centers[:, 0] - radii))\n    boundary_violations_y = jnp.maximum(0, centers[:, 1] + radii - 1) + jnp.maximum(0, - (centers[:, 1] - radii))\n    boundary_penalty = jnp.sum(boundary_violations_x + boundary_violations_y)\n\n    # Negative radii penalty\n    neg_radii_penalty = jnp.sum(jnp.maximum(0, -radii))\n\n    return penalty_weight * (overlap_penalty + boundary_penalty + neg_radii_penalty)\n\ndef\
    \ total_loss_fn(x):\n    return objective_fn(x) + penalty_fn(x)\n\n# --- PGD Optimizer ---\n@jit\ndef pgd_update_step(x, learning_rate):\n    g = grad(total_loss_fn)(x)\n    x_new = x - learning_rate * g\n\n    # Projection step: enforce bounds\n    centers_flat = x_new[:N_CIRCLES*2]\n    radii = x_new[N_CIRCLES*2:]\n    centers_flat = jnp.clip(centers_flat, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6)\n    radii = jnp.clip(radii, 1e-6, 0.5)\n\n    return jnp.hstack([centers_flat, radii])\n\ndef construct_packing_pgd() -> tuple:\n    n_starts = 64\n    n_steps = 2000\n    learning_rate = 1e-4\n\n    master_key = random.PRNGKey(42)\n\n    initial_xs = create_seeds(master_key, n_starts)\n\n    def optimization_body(xs, _):\n        vmapped_update = vmap(pgd_update_step, in_axes=(0, None))\n        xs = vmapped_update(xs, learning_rate)\n        return xs, None\n\n    final_xs, _ = jax.lax.scan(optimization_body, initial_xs, None, length=n_steps)\n\n    final_penalties = vmap(penalty_fn, in_axes=(0, None))(final_xs,\
    \ 1.0)\n    final_scores = vmap(objective_fn)(final_xs)\n\n    combined_metric = final_penalties * 1e6 + final_scores\n\n    best_idx = jnp.argmin(combined_metric)\n    best_x = final_xs[best_idx]\n\n    centers = best_x[:N_CIRCLES*2].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n    radii = best_x[N_CIRCLES*2:]\n    radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n\n    return np.asarray(centers), np.asarray(radii)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
