tick: 405
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis V in the Research Counter. My first attempt at modernizing the PGD method, submission #654, has failed.\n\nThis is a valuable negative result. The error message is clear: \"Circle 0 ... is outside the unit square.\" This indicates a failure in enforcing the boundary constraints. Reviewing my code, I see the likely cause. In `pgd_utils.py`, my projection step for the centers is `jnp.clip(centers_flat, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6)`. This clips the *center* coordinates, but it does not prevent a situation where `center - radius < 0` or `center + radius > 1`. The penalty function is meant to handle this, but if the final penalty weight isn't high enough or the optimizer can't satisfy the penalty, it can produce an invalid solution.\n\nThe fundamental issue is that the projection step is insufficient. It only enforces part of the boundary constraint. I need a more robust method.\n\nMy plan is to fix this in two ways:\n1.  **Improve the Projection:** I will modify the projection step\
    \ in `pgd_utils.py` to be more intelligent. Instead of just clipping the centers, I will also clip them based on their corresponding radii, ensuring `radius <= center <= 1 - radius`.\n2.  **Increase Final Penalty:** I will significantly increase the `penalty_final` hyperparameter in my submission script to more strongly discourage any residual constraint violations at the end of the optimization.\n\nThis iterative debugging and refinement process is central to research. I will first update the utility script with the improved projection logic.\n\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/pgd_utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # pgd_utils.py\n  # An improved JAX-native Projected Gradient Descent (PGD) optimizer.\n  # Developed by Praxis V, based on the abandoned work of Praxis II.\n  # v2: Corrects the projection step to properly enforce boundary constraints.\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import jit, vmap, grad\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  # --- JAX-native Objective and\
    \ Penalty Functions ---\n  def objective_fn(x):\n      radii = x[N_CIRCLES*2:]\n      return -jnp.sum(radii)\n\n  @jit\n  def penalty_fn(x):\n      \"\"\"Calculates the constraint violation penalty for a single configuration.\"\"\"\n      centers = x[:N_CIRCLES*2].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n      radii = x[N_CIRCLES*2:]\n\n      # Pairwise overlap penalty\n      dist_sq = jnp.sum((centers[:, jnp.newaxis, :] - centers[jnp.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n      I, J = jnp.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, 1)\n      overlaps = jnp.maximum(0, (radii[I] + radii[J])**2 - dist_sq[I, J])\n      overlap_penalty = jnp.sum(overlaps)\n\n      # Boundary violation penalty\n      boundary_violations_x = jnp.maximum(0, centers[:, 0] + radii - 1)**2 + jnp.maximum(0, -(centers[:, 0] - radii))**2\n      boundary_violations_y = jnp.maximum(0, centers[:, 1] + radii - 1)**2 + jnp.maximum(0, -(centers[:, 1] - radii))**2\n      boundary_penalty = jnp.sum(boundary_violations_x + boundary_violations_y)\n\n      # Negative radii\
    \ penalty\n      neg_radii_penalty = jnp.sum(jnp.maximum(0, -radii)**2)\n\n      return overlap_penalty + boundary_penalty + neg_radii_penalty\n\n  # --- PGD Optimizer with Annealing ---\n  def get_total_loss_fn(penalty_weight):\n      \"\"\"Creates the total loss function with a specific penalty weight.\"\"\"\n      def total_loss(x):\n          return objective_fn(x) + penalty_weight * penalty_fn(x)\n      return total_loss\n\n  def run_pgd_optimization(initial_xs, n_steps, lr_initial, lr_final, penalty_initial, penalty_final):\n      \"\"\"\n      Runs a full PGD optimization loop with learning rate and penalty weight annealing.\n      \"\"\"\n      lr_schedule = jnp.linspace(lr_initial, lr_final, n_steps)\n      penalty_schedule = jnp.linspace(penalty_initial, penalty_final, n_steps)\n\n      def optimization_step(xs, i):\n          lr = lr_schedule[i]\n          penalty_weight = penalty_schedule[i]\n          \n          grad_fn = jit(grad(get_total_loss_fn(penalty_weight)))\n \
    \         vmapped_grads = vmap(grad_fn)(xs)\n          \n          xs_new = xs - lr * vmapped_grads\n          \n          # --- Corrected Projection Step (v2) ---\n          centers_new = xs_new[:, :N_CIRCLES*2].reshape(-1, N_CIRCLES, 2)\n          radii_new = xs_new[:, N_CIRCLES*2:]\n\n          # First, clip radii to be valid\n          radii_clipped = jnp.clip(radii_new, 1e-6, 0.5)\n\n          # Second, clip centers based on the clipped radii\n          # lower_bound = radii_clipped\n          # upper_bound = 1.0 - radii_clipped\n          # Using jnp.transpose to align shapes for broadcasting\n          centers_clipped = jnp.clip(centers_new, radii_clipped[..., None], 1.0 - radii_clipped[..., None])\n          \n          return jnp.hstack([centers_clipped.reshape(xs.shape[0], -1), radii_clipped])\n\n      @jit\n      def scan_body(carry, i):\n          new_carry = optimization_step(carry, i)\n          return new_carry, None\n\n      final_xs, _ = jax.lax.scan(scan_body, initial_xs,\
    \ jnp.arange(n_steps))\n      \n      return final_xs\n```"
