tick: 406
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis V, located in the Research Counter. I have just updated `pgd_utils.py` with a corrected projection step to properly enforce boundary constraints, which was the cause of failure in my previous submission.\n\nNow, I will resubmit the experiment, incorporating the second part of my debugging plan: increasing the final penalty weight. The corrected projection provides a hard guarantee against boundary violations, but a stronger penalty will better guide the optimizer away from near-violation states and help it resolve overlaps more effectively.\n\nThis iterative process of hypothesizing, testing, analyzing failure, and refining is the core of the scientific method outlined in the Codex. This next submission will test if the combination of a correct projection and a stronger penalty schedule can produce a valid, high-quality packing using the PGD paradigm.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Modernized PGD v2: Corrected Projection & Stronger Penalty\"\ntags: [\"\
    pgd\", \"jax\", \"debug\", \"penalty-method\", \"annealing\"]\nabstract: \"This submission is a second attempt to establish a modernized PGD baseline. It uses the v2 `pgd_utils.py` script, which features a corrected projection step to strictly enforce boundary constraints. Additionally, the final penalty weight in the annealing schedule has been significantly increased to better resolve overlaps. This experiment aims to produce a valid packing and demonstrate the viability of the PGD approach.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import vmap, random\n\n  # Add lineage storage to path to import our corrected utility\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from pgd_utils import run_pgd_optimization, penalty_fn\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def create_random_seeds(key, n_starts):\n      \"\"\"Generates simple random starting configurations.\"\"\"\n      keys = random.split(key, n_starts)\n      \n      @vmap\n      def _create_seed(subkey):\n\
    \          centers = random.uniform(subkey, (N_CIRCLES, 2), minval=0.1, maxval=0.9)\n          radii = jnp.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.05)\n          return jnp.hstack([centers.flatten(), radii])\n          \n      return _create_seed(keys)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # --- Hyperparameters ---\n      n_starts = 128\n      n_steps = 5000\n      \n      lr_initial = 5e-4\n      lr_final = 1e-5\n      \n      # Increased final penalty weight to strongly enforce constraints\n      penalty_initial = 10.0\n      penalty_final = 10000.0 # Increased from 2000.0\n      \n      master_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n      \n      # --- Execution ---\n      initial_xs = create_random_seeds(master_key, n_starts)\n      \n      final_xs = run_pgd_optimization(\n          initial_xs, \n          n_steps, \n          lr_initial, \n          lr_final, \n          penalty_initial, \n          penalty_final\n      )\n      \n      # --- Selection ---\n      final_penalties = vmap(penalty_fn)(final_xs)\n\
    \      final_scores = -vmap(lambda x: jnp.sum(x[N_CIRCLES*2:]))(final_xs)\n      \n      valid_mask = final_penalties < 1e-6\n      \n      if jnp.any(valid_mask):\n          best_idx = jnp.argmax(jnp.where(valid_mask, final_scores, -jnp.inf))\n      else:\n          best_idx = jnp.argmin(final_penalties)\n\n      best_x = final_xs[best_idx]\n      \n      # --- Formatting ---\n      centers = np.asarray(best_x[:N_CIRCLES*2].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      radii = np.asarray(best_x[N_CIRCLES*2:])\n      \n      return centers, radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n```"
