parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 408\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the SOTA from Praxis IV, my focus is to explore fundamentally new research paradigms beyond local optimization to discover a higher-performing class of solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 71,753 / 300,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 30 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Modernized PGD v3: Farthest-Point\
    \ Seeding' (ID: 659) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6764411926269531\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 0.676441\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 659\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed broadcasting error in FPS seed generation. Code now runs successfully and achieves score of 0.6764.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a NumPy broadcasting error on line 22 of the `_create_single_fps_seed` function:\n\n```python\ndist_to_existing = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - points[:i, np.newaxis])**2, axis=2)\n```\n\nThe issue was with the shape mismatch:\n- `candidates[:, np.newaxis, :]` has shape `(2000, 1, 2)`\n- `points[:i, np.newaxis]` has shape `(i, 1, 2)`\n\nFor proper broadcasting to compute distances from 2000 candidates to `i` existing points, we need:\n- `candidates[:, np.newaxis, :]` with shape `(2000, 1, 2)`\n- `points[np.newaxis, :i, :]` with shape `(1, i, 2)`\n\nThis allows the\
    \ subtraction to broadcast to `(2000, i, 2)`, representing distances from each candidate to each existing point.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 22 from:\n```python\ndist_to_existing = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - points[:i, np.newaxis])**2, axis=2)\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\ndist_to_existing = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - points[np.newaxis, :i, :])**2, axis=2)\n```\n\nThe key change is `points[:i, np.newaxis]` → `points[np.newaxis, :i, :]` which correctly positions the newaxis dimension to enable broadcasting.\n\n## Result\n- Fixed code successfully executes without crashes\n- Achieves score of 0.6764411926269531\n- The Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS) seeding strategy now works as intended, generating diverse initial configurations for the PGD optimization\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\n\
    import numpy as np\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import vmap, random\n\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom pgd_utils import run_pgd_optimization, penalty_fn\n\nN_CIRCLES = 32\n\ndef create_fps_seeds(key, n_starts):\n    \"\"\"Generates starting configurations using Farthest-Point Sampling.\"\"\"\n    keys = random.split(key, n_starts)\n\n    def _create_single_fps_seed(subkey):\n        \"\"\"Generates one FPS seed using NumPy for simplicity.\"\"\"\n        # Use subkey to seed a NumPy RNG for deterministic but diverse starts\n        np_rng = np.random.default_rng(int(subkey[0]))\n\n        points = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n        points[0] = np_rng.uniform(0.05, 0.95, 2)\n\n        min_dists = np.full(N_CIRCLES, np.inf)\n\n        for i in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n            dist_sq = np.sum((points[:i, np.newaxis, :] - points[np.newaxis, :i, :])**2, axis=-1)\n            last_point_dists = np.sum((points[i-1] - points[:i-1])**2, axis=1)\n            min_dists[:i-1]\
    \ = np.minimum(min_dists[:i-1], last_point_dists)\n\n            # Sample candidates and find the one farthest from existing points\n            num_candidates = 2000\n            candidates = np_rng.uniform(0.05, 0.95, (num_candidates, 2))\n\n            # Fixed broadcasting: candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] has shape (2000, 1, 2)\n            # points[:i] has shape (i, 2), so we need (1, i, 2) to broadcast correctly\n            dist_to_existing = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - points[np.newaxis, :i, :])**2, axis=2)\n            min_dist_to_existing = np.min(dist_to_existing, axis=1)\n\n            points[i] = candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_to_existing)]\n\n        radii = jnp.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.05)\n        return jnp.hstack([jnp.array(points).flatten(), radii])\n\n    # Although the inner function uses NumPy, we can still vmap it with JAX\n    # by wrapping it in jax.pure_callback. For this test, a simple loop is sufficient and clearer.\n    seeds = [_create_single_fps_seed(k)\
    \ for k in keys]\n    return jnp.stack(seeds)\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # --- Hyperparameters ---\n    n_starts = 128\n    n_steps = 5000\n    lr_initial = 5e-4\n    lr_final = 1e-5\n    penalty_initial = 10.0\n    penalty_final = 10000.0\n\n    master_key = random.PRNGKey(1) # Changed seed for new method\n\n    # --- Execution ---\n    initial_xs = create_fps_seeds(master_key, n_starts)\n\n    final_xs = run_pgd_optimization(\n        initial_xs, n_steps, lr_initial, lr_final, penalty_initial, penalty_final\n    )\n\n    # --- Selection ---\n    final_penalties = vmap(penalty_fn)(final_xs)\n    final_scores = -vmap(lambda x: jnp.sum(x[N_CIRCLES*2:]))(final_xs)\n\n    valid_mask = final_penalties < 1e-6\n\n    if jnp.any(valid_mask):\n        best_idx = jnp.argmax(jnp.where(valid_mask, final_scores, -jnp.inf))\n    else:\n        best_idx = jnp.argmin(final_penalties)\n\n    best_x = final_xs[best_idx]\n\n    # --- Formatting ---\n    centers = np.asarray(best_x[:N_CIRCLES*2].reshape(N_CIRCLES,\
    \ 2))\n    radii = np.asarray(best_x[N_CIRCLES*2:])\n\n    return centers, radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Modernized PGD v3: Farthest-Point Seeding' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 659.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 659 | 1 | Modernized PGD v3: Farthest-Point Seeding | Praxis V | 407 | 0.6764412 |\n| 657 | 1 | Modernized PGD v2: Corrected Projection & Stronger Penalty | Praxis V | 406 | 0.6793420 |\n| 654 | 1 | Modernized PGD v1: Annealing Penalty & LR Schedule | Praxis V | 404 | 0.0000000 |\n| 646 | 1 | Validation: Standalone ASN Refinement on SOTA Artifact | Praxis V | 397 | 2.9395728 |\n| 617 | 1 | Hybrid Non-Local Search: Adaptive Jiggle & Refine | Praxis IV | 374 | 2.9395728 |\n| 610 | 1 | Baseline for Paper: Original SLSQP Adaptive Search | Praxis IV | 365 | 2.9365263 |\n| 598 | 1 | Non-Local Search v2: Parameterized Pair Rotation | Praxis IV | 359 | 2.9395728 |\n| 595 | 1 | Non-Local Search v1: Tightest Pair Rotation | Praxis IV | 358 | 2.8893761 |\n| 590 | 1 | MM-LP+ASN v1: Refinement of SOTA Artifact | Praxis IV | 355 | 2.9395728 |\n| 588 | 1 | Unit Test v3.2 (Debug): ASN Step with Normalization | Praxis IV | 354 | 2.9395728 |\n\nPage 1 of 15 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
