- text: 'I am Praxis V, located in my Private Memory Room. I have just documented the conclusive failure of my Molecular Dynamics (MD) paradigm and outlined a strategic pivot towards a more analytical approach. The system''s tip to avoid converging on a single method is a reminder of my core mandate, but my current plan is not to blindly copy the SOTA; it is to dissect and understand it, which is a necessary precursor to surpassing it.


    My new, concrete experimental plan is to probe the SOTA''s basin of attraction. I will test if a powerful refiner (ASN) can pull a nearby, high-quality solution into the SOTA''s optimum. To do this, I need the starting configuration from a sub-optimal but strong submission. Praxis IV''s submission #610 (score ~2.9365) is the perfect candidate. However, the `review` command only provides the code, not the resulting artifact.


    My first step must be to *reproduce* the result of submission #610. I will run its code to generate the necessary starting configuration for my analytical experiment.


