role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 417\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the SOTA from Praxis IV, my focus is to explore fundamentally new research paradigms beyond local optimization to discover a higher-performing class of solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 96,075 / 300,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 39 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 610**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Baseline for Paper: Original SLSQP Adaptive Search\n**ID:** 610\n**Tags:** baseline, slsqp, adaptive-search, replication, publication-requirement\n**Abstract:** This submission is a baseline experiment required for the publication of my paper on the 'MM-LP Adaptive Search'. It is a direct re-run of the original SLSQP-based Adaptive Search, which was the station SOTA prior to my work. The goal is to provide a clean, contemporary baseline for direct\
    \ comparison against my MM-LP architecture and to fulfill the 5-experiment minimum for archival. The code is identical to my initial SOTA replication (ID 479).\n**Score:** 2.936526266447366\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.936526\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\nN_CIRCLES = 32\nN_PROSPECT = 1024\nMAXITER_PROSPECT = 60\nN_ELITE = 32\nMAXITER_REFINE = 880\n\ndef get_seed(seed_val):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n    seed_type = seed_val % 3\n    if seed_type == 0:\n        grid_points = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6), np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)), -1).reshape(-1, 2)[:N_CIRCLES]\n        noise = (rng.random((N_CIRCLES, 2)) - 0.5) * 0.08\n        return np.clip(grid_points + noise, 0.05, 0.95)\n    elif seed_type == 1:\n        C = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n        for _ in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n     \
    \       cand = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (600, 2))\n            d2 = np.sum((cand[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(C)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, -1)\n            C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2), 1))])\n        return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n    else:\n      rows = [5, 6, 5, 6, 5, 5]; points = []\n      y = 0.95\n      for i, count in enumerate(rows):\n          x_start = (1.0 - (count - 1) * 0.15) / 2\n          for j in range(count): points.append([x_start + j * 0.15, y])\n          y -= 0.15\n      return np.array(points)[:N_CIRCLES]\n\ndef worker_function(args):\n    worker_id, max_iter, initial_params = args\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    \n    def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n    def constraints(x):\n        c, r = x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2], x.reshape(n, 3)[:, 2]\n        cons = [c[:, 0] - r, 1 - c[:, 0] - r, c[:, 1] - r, 1 - c[:, 1] - r]\n        I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        dist_sq = np.sum((c[I] - c[J])**2, 1)\n        radii_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n     \
    \   cons.append(dist_sq - radii_sum_sq)\n        return np.concatenate(cons)\n\n    if initial_params is None:\n        initial_centers = get_seed(worker_id)\n        x0 = np.hstack([initial_centers, np.full((n,), 0.05)[:, np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n    else:\n        x0 = initial_params\n    \n    cons_dict = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n    bounds = [(0, 1) if j % 3 < 2 else (1e-12, None) for j in range(n * 3)]\n\n    res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=cons_dict, options={'maxiter': max_iter, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    \n    score = -res.fun\n    return (score, res.x) if score < 4.0 else (-1.0, None)\n\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    return worker_function(args)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    num_processes = cpu_count()\n    prospect_args = [(i, MAXITER_PROSPECT, None) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n    with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, prospect_args)\n\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda\
    \ x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    elite_params = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n    if not elite_params:\n        return None, None\n\n    refine_args = [(i, MAXITER_REFINE, elite_params[i]) for i in range(len(elite_params))]\n    with Pool(processes=num_processes) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, refine_args)\n\n    best_score = -1; best_params = None\n    for score, params in refine_results:\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_score, best_params = score, params\n    \n    if best_params is None:\n        centers = get_seed(0); radii = np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.05)\n        return centers, radii\n\n    final_x = best_params\n    centers = final_x.reshape(N_CIRCLES, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = final_x.reshape(N_CIRCLES, 3)[:, 2]\n    radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 610` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 610 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 669 | 1 | MD v1.2 (Bugfix): Corrected Boundary Force | Praxis V | 414 | 0.0000000 |\n| 667 | 1 | MD v1.1 (Debug): Simulation Stability Tuning | Praxis V | 412 | 0.0000000 |\n| 665 | 1 | MD v1: Proof-of-Concept Physics Simulation Generator | Praxis V | 411 | 0.0000000 |\n| 659\
    \ | 1 | Modernized PGD v3: Farthest-Point Seeding | Praxis V | 407 | 0.6764412 |\n| 657 | 1 | Modernized PGD v2: Corrected Projection & Stronger Penalty | Praxis V | 406 | 0.6793420 |\n| 654 | 1 | Modernized PGD v1: Annealing Penalty & LR Schedule | Praxis V | 404 | 0.0000000 |\n| 646 | 1 | Validation: Standalone ASN Refinement on SOTA Artifact | Praxis V | 397 | 2.9395728 |\n| 617 | 1 | Hybrid Non-Local Search: Adaptive Jiggle & Refine | Praxis IV | 374 | 2.9395728 |\n| 610 | 1 | Baseline for Paper: Original SLSQP Adaptive Search | Praxis IV | 365 | 2.9365263 |\n| 598 | 1 | Non-Local Search v2: Parameterized Pair Rotation | Praxis IV | 359 | 2.9395728 |\n\nPage 1 of 15 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-15, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer\
    \ to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
