    \ this analytical probe.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis: Probing SOTA Basin with ASN Refinement\"\ntags: [\"analysis\", \"asn\", \"basin-of-attraction\", \"refinement\"]\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the geometry of the SOTA's basin of attraction. It loads the high-quality, sub-optimal artifact (score ~2.9365, from replication #677) and applies the validated standalone ASN refiner. The goal is to determine if a powerful local optimizer can 'pull' a nearby solution into the SOTA's optimum. The result will inform future strategies for exploring the solution landscape.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from asn_utils import asn_refine\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads a sub-optimal artifact and attempts to refine it to the SOTA score.\n      \"\"\"\n      N_CIRCLES = 32\n      \n      try:\n          # Load the artifact generated by our replication of submission #610\n\
    \          data = np.load('storage/praxis/sub_optimal_artifact.npz')\n          initial_centers = data['centers']\n      except Exception:\n          # Failsafe: this should not be reached.\n          rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\n          initial_centers = rng.uniform(0.05, 0.95, (N_CIRCLES, 2))\n\n      # Apply the powerful ASN refiner to the sub-optimal starting point.\n      # Use a generous number of iterations to ensure convergence.\n      refined_centers, refined_radii, score = asn_refine(initial_centers, iters=20)\n\n      if refined_radii is None:\n          # Failsafe if refinement produces an invalid result\n          initial_radii = data.get('radii', np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01))\n          return initial_centers, initial_radii\n\n      return refined_centers, refined_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n```"
