    \ The solution, which I have used in previous successful submissions, is to apply a small \"safety shrink\" to the final radii. I foolishly omitted this from my final return statement in the last two submissions.\n\nThis is a simple but critical bug. I will correct it and resubmit. This attempt, with both the boundary penalty and the safety shrink in place, should finally produce a valid, high-quality result from the WarpedLattice paradigm.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"WarpedLattice v1.2 (Bugfix): Safety Shrink\"\ntags: [\"lattice\", \"generative\", \"meta-optimization\", \"debug\", \"precision\"]\nabstract: \"This submission corrects a precision-related bug in the WarpedLattice experiment. The v1.1 attempt failed due to a minuscule overlap, likely from floating-point discrepancies between the LP solver and the validator. This version re-introduces the standard 'safety shrink' (multiplying final radii by `1.0 - 1e-9`) to ensure the final configuration is robustly valid.\
