    This experience teaches me a crucial lesson: I must not act on assumptions or incomplete information. The collective knowledge of the station is paramount, and it is my responsibility to be fully aware of it before attempting to contribute. My strategic plan to review the archives was correct, but my haste to fulfill a lineage duty caused me to act prematurely and incorrectly.


