parts:
- text: 'I am Praxis V in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, #712, which tested a dimensionality reduction strategy for my WarpedLattice paradigm, has failed to produce a significant improvement. In fact, the score regressed slightly.


    This is a definitive result. I have now tested the "Crystallographic Optimization" concept with a simple hill-climber, a global optimizer on a high-dimensional space, and a global optimizer on a reduced-dimensionality space. All have produced valid but extremely poor-quality packings. The consistent failure across these varied implementations provides strong evidence that the core hypothesis is flawed. The assumption that a globally optimal packing can be represented as a smooth, low-parameter deformation of a perfect lattice appears to be incorrect for this specific problem (n=32 in a square). The necessary structure is likely more complex, involving defects or multiple crystalline domains, which my simple parameterizations cannot capture.


    I am officially declaring this entire line of research—the WarpedLattice/Crystallographic Optimization paradigm—a failure. I have pursued it rigorously, and the negative results are now conclusive.


    It is time for a complete strategic reset. I have spent my entire tenure thus far pursuing novel generative methods from first principles, and all have failed. My mandate from my predecessor was to explore new paradigms, and I have done so. But my duty is also to achieve a high score and contribute to the station''s progress. My current approach is not achieving this.


    The leaderboard shows that agents like Verity II, Cogitator I, and Athena I are making progress with methods that are refinements and hybrids of the established SOTA architectures (MM-LP, Adaptive Search). I will now pivot my strategy to align with the successful methodologies in the station. I will stop my independent, from-scratch work and begin a new research arc focused on mastering, replicating, and ultimately improving upon the current SOTA MM-LP Adaptive Search framework.


    My first step is to go to the Reflection Chamber to formally document this major strategic pivot and outline my new research program.


    /execute_action{goto reflect}'
