tick: 443
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis V in the Research Counter. I have just created the `mmlp_utils.py` script, which contains my from-scratch implementation of the core MM-LP center-update logic. This is the first major step in Phase 1 of my new research program.\n\nThe next step is to build the full \"MM-LP Adaptive Search\" framework around this new utility. This framework, pioneered by the Cognito lineage, involves a two-stage search: a broad \"prospecting\" stage with many short runs, followed by a deep \"refining\" stage on the best candidates.\n\nI will now write and submit the first version of my SOTA replication attempt. This script will import my new `mmlp_utils.py` and my trusted `asn_utils.py` (for its exact LP solver) and orchestrate the full two-stage search. I will use seeding strategies and hyperparameters informed by my review of the public archives. The goal of this submission is to get a first signal on the correctness of my implementation and to begin the iterative debugging process\
    \ required to match the SOTA score.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Replication v1: MM-LP Adaptive Search from Scratch\"\ntags: [\"sota-replication\", \"mm-lp\", \"adaptive-search\", \"praxis-v\"]\nabstract: \"This is the first attempt in a new research program to replicate the SOTA MM-LP Adaptive Search framework from scratch, based on public specifications. This submission uses the new `mmlp_utils.py` for center updates and the proven LP solver from `asn_utils.py` for scoring. It implements the full two-stage (prospecting/refining) search architecture. The goal is to begin the iterative process of validating this from-scratch implementation against the known SOTA score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from mmlp_utils import mmlp_center_update\n  from asn_utils import solve_radii_lp_with_duals # For exact scoring\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def get_fps_seed(seed_val):\n\
    \      \"\"\"Generates one Farthest-Point Sampling seed.\"\"\"\n      np_rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n      points = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2))\n      points[0] = np_rng.uniform(0.05, 0.95, 2)\n      \n      for i in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n          num_candidates = 2000\n          candidates = np_rng.uniform(0.05, 0.95, (num_candidates, 2))\n          dist_to_existing = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - points[np.newaxis, :i, :])**2, axis=2)\n          min_dist_to_existing = np.min(dist_to_existing, axis=1)\n          points[i] = candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_to_existing)]\n      return points\n\n  def run_mmlp_optimization(args):\n      \"\"\"Worker function to run an MM-LP optimization from a given seed.\"\"\"\n      initial_centers, num_iters, initial_delta = args\n      \n      centers_best = initial_centers.copy()\n      \n      lp_res = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers_best)\n      if lp_res is None: return (-1.0, None)\n      score_best = np.sum(lp_res['radii'])\n\
    \      radii_best = lp_res['radii']\n\n      centers_anchor = centers_best.copy()\n      radii_anchor = radii_best.copy()\n      delta = initial_delta\n\n      for _ in range(num_iters):\n          # Perform one MM-LP step\n          update_res = mmlp_center_update(centers_anchor, radii_anchor, delta)\n          \n          if update_res is None:\n              delta *= 0.8 # Shrink trust region on failure\n              continue\n\n          candidate_centers = update_res['centers']\n          \n          # Evaluate the new centers with the exact LP solver\n          exact_lp_res = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(candidate_centers)\n          if exact_lp_res is None:\n              delta *= 0.8\n              continue\n              \n          score_candidate = np.sum(exact_lp_res['radii'])\n\n          # Accept-on-Strict-Improvement\n          if score_candidate > score_best:\n              score_best = score_candidate\n              centers_best = candidate_centers\n              radii_best\
    \ = exact_lp_res['radii']\n              centers_anchor = centers_best.copy()\n              radii_anchor = radii_best.copy()\n              delta = min(0.05, delta * 1.2) # Grow trust region on success\n          else:\n              delta *= 0.8\n\n      return (score_best, centers_best)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      N_PROSPECT = 1024\n      N_ELITE = 32\n      PROSPECT_ITER = 20\n      REFINE_ITER = 100\n      DELTA0 = 0.015\n\n      # --- Stage 1: Prospecting ---\n      prospect_seeds = [get_fps_seed(i) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n      prospect_args = [(seed, PROSPECT_ITER, DELTA0) for seed in prospect_seeds]\n      \n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(run_mmlp_optimization, prospect_args)\n\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n\n      if not elite_centers:\n          return get_fps_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,),\
    \ 0.01)\n\n      # --- Stage 2: Refining ---\n      refine_args = [(centers, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0) for centers in elite_centers]\n      \n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(run_mmlp_optimization, refine_args)\n      \n      best_score = -1.0\n      best_centers = None\n      for score, centers in refine_results:\n          if score > best_score:\n              best_score = score\n              best_centers = centers\n\n      if best_centers is None:\n          return get_fps_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n      # Final, definitive radii calculation\n      final_lp_res = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)\n      final_radii = final_lp_res['radii']\n\n      return best_centers, final_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n```"
