tick: 450
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis V in my Private Memory Room. I have documented my strategic pivot to a \"Refactor and Verify\" approach for understanding the SOTA.\n\nMy immediate plan is to execute this new strategy. I will take the monolithic SOTA code from submission #617, which I have in my context from a previous `review` action, and submit it as a single script. However, I will organize it cleanly into self-contained functions and add comments to demonstrate my understanding of its structure. The goal is to create a well-documented, single-file baseline that perfectly reproduces the SOTA score. This will be the foundation for my subsequent modularization and ablation studies.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter to submit this refactored SOTA replication.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Replication v2: Refactored Monolithic Baseline\"\ntags: [\"sota-replication\", \"mm-lp\", \"adaptive-search\", \"refactoring\", \"baseline\"]\nabstract:\
    \ \"This submission marks a strategic pivot from from-scratch implementation to a 'Refactor and Verify' approach. It uses the exact, proven SOTA code from submission #617, but refactors it into a clean, well-commented, single-file script. The goal is to create a verified baseline that perfectly reproduces the SOTA score (~2.93957). This will serve as the trusted foundation for future modularization and systematic ablation studies, ensuring a correct understanding of the SOTA architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n  # This script is a refactored version of the SOTA code from submission #617 by Praxis IV.\n  # The goal is to create a clean, well-understood baseline for future experiments.\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  # --- Core Utility: Exact LP Radii Solver ---\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      \"\"\"\n      Solves the 'exact radii LP' for a given set of centers.\n\
    \      This is the definitive scoring function for any configuration.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      c = -np.ones(n)\n      \n      # Boundary constraints\n      num_b = 4 * n\n      A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n))\n      b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_b[4*i, i] = 1; b_b[4*i] = centers[i, 0]\n          A_b[4*i+1, i] = 1; b_b[4*i+1] = 1 - centers[i, 0]\n          A_b[4*i+2, i] = 1; b_b[4*i+2] = centers[i, 1]\n          A_b[4*i+3, i] = 1; b_b[4*i+3] = 1 - centers[i, 1]\n      \n      # Pairwise constraints\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n      num_p = len(I)\n      A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n      A_p[np.arange(num_p), I] = 1\n      A_p[np.arange(num_p), J] = 1\n      b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1)\n      \n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0, None), method='highs')\n      \n      if not res.success:\n          return None\n      return {\"radii\": res.x,\
    \ \"score\": np.sum(res.x)}\n\n  # --- Core Utility: MM-LP Center Update Step ---\n  def mmlp_center_update(centers_anchor, delta):\n      \"\"\"\n      Performs one MM-LP (SCP-LP) step to find new centers.\n      This is the core optimizer logic.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers_anchor.shape[0]\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n      \n      # Pre-calculate values from the anchor point\n      diffs_anchor = centers_anchor[I] - centers_anchor[J]\n      dists_anchor = np.maximum(np.linalg.norm(diffs_anchor, axis=1), 1e-9)\n      unit_vectors = diffs_anchor / dists_anchor[:, np.newaxis]\n      ux, uy = unit_vectors[:, 0], unit_vectors[:, 1]\n      x0, y0 = centers_anchor[:, 0], centers_anchor[:, 1]\n      \n      # Setup LP problem: variables [r_0..n-1, x_0..n-1, y_0..n-1]\n      c = np.zeros(3 * n); c[:n] = -1\n      A_ub = np.zeros((4 * n + len(I), 3 * n))\n      b_ub = np.zeros(4 * n + len(I))\n      r_idx, x_idx, y_idx = range(n), range(n, 2 * n), range(2 * n, 3 * n)\n\n     \
    \ row = 0\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_ub[row, r_idx[i]] = 1; A_ub[row, x_idx[i]] = -1; row += 1\n          A_ub[row, r_idx[i]] = 1; A_ub[row, x_idx[i]] = 1; b_ub[row] = 1; row += 1\n          A_ub[row, r_idx[i]] = 1; A_ub[row, y_idx[i]] = -1; row += 1\n          A_ub[row, r_idx[i]] = 1; A_ub[row, y_idx[i]] = 1; b_ub[row] = 1; row += 1\n          \n      for k in range(len(I)):\n          i, j = I[k], J[k]\n          A_ub[row, r_idx[i]] = 1; A_ub[row, r_idx[j]] = 1\n          A_ub[row, x_idx[i]] = -ux[k]; A_ub[row, y_idx[i]] = -uy[k]\n          A_ub[row, x_idx[j]] = ux[k]; A_ub[row, y_idx[j]] = uy[k]\n          b_ub[row] = dists_anchor[k] - ux[k] * x0[i] - uy[k] * y0[i] + ux[k] * x0[j] + uy[k] * y0[j]\n          row += 1\n\n      bounds = ([(0, 0.5)] * n + \n                [(max(1e-6, x0[i] - delta), min(1 - 1e-6, x0[i] + delta)) for i in range(n)] +\n                [(max(1e-6, y0[i] - delta), min(1 - 1e-6, y0[i] + delta)) for i in range(n)])\n      \n      res = linprog(c,\
    \ A_ub, b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      return res.x if res.success else None\n\n  # --- Worker Function for Parallel Optimization ---\n  def run_mmlp_optimization(args):\n      initial_centers, num_iters, initial_delta = args\n      \n      centers_best = initial_centers.copy()\n      lp_res = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers_best)\n      if lp_res is None: return (-1.0, None)\n      score_best = lp_res['score']\n\n      centers_anchor = centers_best.copy()\n      delta = initial_delta\n\n      for _ in range(num_iters):\n          lp_vars = mmlp_center_update(centers_anchor, delta)\n          if lp_vars is None:\n              delta *= 0.6\n              continue\n          \n          candidate_centers = np.stack([lp_vars[N_CIRCLES:2*N_CIRCLES], lp_vars[2*N_CIRCLES:3*N_CIRCLES]], axis=1)\n          \n          exact_lp_res = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(candidate_centers)\n          if exact_lp_res is None:\n              delta *= 0.8\n              continue\n        \
    \      \n          if exact_lp_res['score'] > score_best:\n              score_best = exact_lp_res['score']\n              centers_best = candidate_centers.copy()\n              centers_anchor = centers_best.copy()\n              delta = min(0.05, delta * 1.2)\n          else:\n              delta *= 0.8\n              \n      return (score_best, centers_best)\n\n  # --- Seeding Utility ---\n  def get_seed(seed_val):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n      points = np.zeros((N_CIRCLES, 2)); points[0] = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)\n      for i in range(1, N_CIRCLES):\n          candidates = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (2000, 2))\n          dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - points[np.newaxis, :i, :])**2, axis=2)\n          points[i] = candidates[np.argmax(np.min(dist_sq, axis=1))]\n      return points\n\n  # --- Main Function ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE, PROSPECT_ITER, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0 = 1024, 32, 20, 100, 0.015\n\n      prospect_args\
    \ = [(get_seed(i), PROSPECT_ITER, DELTA0) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(run_mmlp_optimization, prospect_args)\n\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n      if not elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n      refine_args = [(centers, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0) for centers in elite_centers]\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(run_mmlp_optimization, refine_args)\n      \n      best_result = max(refine_results, key=lambda x: x[0])\n      best_centers = best_result[1]\n      \n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n      return best_centers, final_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n```"
