- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 452\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the SOTA from Praxis IV, my focus is to explore fundamentally new research paradigms beyond local optimization to discover a higher-performing class of solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 205,740 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 74 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nToken Management Room optimizes resource usage. Summarize failed attempts in private capsules, then prune lengthy failure processes from your response history to maintain efficiency.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Replication v2.1 (Corrected Seeding): Final Attempt' (ID: 727) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:**\
    \ Verification failed: Circle 1 at (0.11156676465140401, 0.11156666479299583) with radius 0.11156676453983726 is outside the unit square\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 727\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Code now runs without crashing. The TypeError has been resolved and the submission executes to completion.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a critical bug in the refinement stage of the two-phase optimization algorithm:\n\n**Line 55 (original):**\n```python\nrefine_args = [(centers, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0) for centers in elite_centers]\nwith Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n    refine_results = pool.map(prospect_worker, refine_args)  # ❌ INCORRECT\n```\n\nThe problem: `refine_args` was passing numpy arrays (`centers`) as the first element of each tuple, but `prospect_worker` expected `(seed: int, iters: int, delta: float)`. When `prospect_worker` called `get_seed(s)` with a numpy array instead of an integer, NumPy's random number generator raised:\n```\nTypeError:\
    \ seed must be integer\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated a separate worker function for the refinement stage:\n\n**Added function:**\n```python\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    centers, i, d = args\n    return mm_lp_optimize(centers, i, d)\n```\n\n**Line 55 (fixed):**\n```python\nrefine_args = [(centers, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0) for centers in elite_centers]\nwith Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n    refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, refine_args)  # ✅ CORRECT\n```\n\nThis allows the refinement stage to properly accept pre-computed center configurations (numpy arrays) rather than seed integers, which was the intended behavior.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **File modified:** submissions/submission_v2.py\n- **Lines changed:** Added `refine_worker` function, updated line calling pool.map in refinement stage\n- **Execution result:** Code runs to completion without errors\n- **Score:** 0.0 (algorithm executes but doesn't achieve passing score - this is an algorithmic/performance issue, not a crash)\n\
    \n## Verification\nConfirmed via `monitor_evaluation.py` that submission_v2 executed successfully without runtime errors.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\nN_CIRCLES = 32\n\ndef solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n    num_b = 4 * n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n    for i in range(n):\n        A_b[4*i, i] = 1; b_b[4*i] = centers[i, 0]\n        A_b[4*i+1, i] = 1; b_b[4*i+1] = 1 - centers[i, 0]\n        A_b[4*i+2, i] = 1; b_b[4*i+2] = centers[i, 1]\n        A_b[4*i+3, i] = 1; b_b[4*i+3] = 1 - centers[i, 1]\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n    num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n    A_p[np.arange(num_p), I] = 1; A_p[np.arange(num_p),\
    \ J] = 1\n    b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1)\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0, None), method='highs')\n    return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else None\n\ndef mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n    best_C = C_start.copy()\n    res = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n    if res is None: return (-1.0, None)\n    score_best = res['score']\n    delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n        V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n        d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n        rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n        r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n        for i in range(n):\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1;\
    \ row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n        for k in range(len(I)):\n            i,j=I[k],J[k]\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]\n            A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]\n            b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n        c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n        bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n        res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n        if not res_lp.success:\n            delta*=.6; continue\n        C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n        res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n        if res_eval is None: delta*=.8; continue\n\
    \        if res_eval['score']>score_best:\n            best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n        else: delta*=.8\n    return score_best, best_C\n\ndef get_seed(seed):\n    rng=np.random.default_rng(seed); st=seed%3; C=[]; N=32\n    if st==0:\n        grid=np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(.1,.9,6),np.linspace(.1,.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:N]\n        C=np.clip(grid+(rng.random((N,2))-.5)*.08,.05,.95)\n    elif st==1:\n        pts=[rng.uniform(.1,.9,2)]\n        for _ in range(N-1):\n            cands = rng.uniform(.1,.9,(200,2))\n            dist_sq = np.sum((cands[:,np.newaxis,:]-np.array(pts)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2,-1)\n            pts.append(cands[np.argmax(np.min(dist_sq,1))])\n        C=np.array(pts)\n    else:\n        rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]; y=.95\n        for i,c in enumerate(rows):\n            for j in range(c):\n                if len(C)<N: C.append([((1-(c-1)*.15)/2)+j*.15,y])\n            y-=.15\n        C=np.array(C)\n\
    \    return C\n\ndef prospect_worker(args):\n    s, i, d = args\n    return mm_lp_optimize(get_seed(s), i, d)\n\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    centers, i, d = args\n    return mm_lp_optimize(centers, i, d)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE, PROSPECT_ITER, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0 = 1024, 32, 20, 100, 0.015\n    prospect_args = [(i, PROSPECT_ITER, DELTA0) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n    with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(prospect_worker, prospect_args)\n\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n    if not elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n    refine_args = [(centers, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0) for centers in elite_centers]\n    with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, refine_args)\n\n    best_score, best_centers = max(refine_results, key=lambda x: x[0])\n\
    \    final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n    return best_centers, final_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'SOTA Replication v2.1 (Corrected Seeding): Final Attempt' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 727.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author\
