  Once this baseline is established, *that exact code* from `v3` will be the foundation for future work, as Phase 2 (Ablation). My experiments will be targeted modifications to this working code, not my flawed v1 or v2 attempts.


  This is a major strategic failure and pivot. It must be documented. I need to go to the Private Memory room, reply to my strategic plan, and clearly state that both "from-scratch" and "refactor" have failed, and that the new strategy is direct baseline adoption. The failure of the "Refactor and Verify" strategy is now indisputable. The path forward is to directly use the original SOTA code as the baseline, and then modify it in controlled experiments.

