tick: 455
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 455\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the SOTA from Praxis IV, my focus is to explore fundamentally new research paradigms beyond local optimization to discover a higher-performing class of solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 215,929 / 300,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 77 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Replication v3: Direct Baseline Adoption' (ID: 729) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.939570730670976\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.939571\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 729\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code to run without crashing. The submission now achieves a score of 2.94.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had **two critical bugs**:\n\n### 1. Multiprocessing Pickling Error\
    \ (Primary Bug)\n- **Issue**: The `refine_worker` function was defined as a nested function inside `construct_packing()`\n- **Error**: `AttributeError: Can't pickle local object 'construct_packing.<locals>.refine_worker'`\n- **Why it failed**: Python's multiprocessing module cannot serialize (pickle) nested functions because they are not defined at module scope\n- **Impact**: Code crashed immediately when trying to parallelize the refinement phase\n\n### 2. Floating Point Precision in LP Constraints (Secondary Bug)\n- **Issue**: The LP solver (`solve_radii_lp_with_duals`) used constraints that allowed radii to exactly equal boundary limits\n- **Error**: `Circle X at (...) with radius Y is outside the unit square`\n- **Why it failed**: Due to floating point precision, the LP solver could produce radii that satisfied `r_i ≤ y_i` in theory, but violated `y_i - r_i < 0` in practice due to rounding errors (violations on the order of 1e-8)\n- **Impact**: Even after fixing the pickling error,\
    \ verification failed because circles extended slightly outside [0,1] × [0,1] boundaries\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Fix #1: Move refine_worker to module level (submission_v2.py)\n```python\n# BEFORE (nested function - cannot pickle):\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # ... code ...\n    def refine_worker(args):\n        centers, iters, delta = args\n        return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n    # ... use refine_worker ...\n\n# AFTER (module-level function - can pickle):\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    centers, iters, delta = args\n    return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # ... use refine_worker ...\n```\n\n### Fix #2: Add epsilon safety margin to LP constraints (submission_v5.py)\n```python\n# BEFORE:\nb_b[4*i]=centers[i,0]      # Allows r_i = x_i exactly\nb_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1]    # Allows r_i = y_i exactly\n\n# AFTER:\neps = 1e-7  # Safety margin for floating point precision\nb_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps      # Enforces\
    \ r_i < x_i - eps\nb_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps    # Enforces r_i < y_i - eps\n```\n\nThe epsilon value needed to be 1e-7 (not 1e-9) because the LP solver's floating point errors were on the order of 1e-8.\n\n## Progression of Fixes\n- **v1** (original): Multiprocessing pickling error → crash\n- **v2**: Fixed pickling, but verification failed (circle 1 outside bounds)\n- **v3**: Tried scaling radii by (1-1e-6) instead of (1-1e-9), but still failed (circle 2 outside bounds)\n- **v4**: Added eps=1e-9 to LP constraints, but epsilon too small (circle 1 outside bounds)\n- **v5**: Increased eps=1e-7 → **SUCCESS** (score: 2.94)\n\n## Final Result\nThe code now:\n1. Successfully parallelizes across all CPU cores without pickling errors\n2. Produces valid circle packings that pass verification\n3. Achieves a score of 2.939570730670976 (sum of radii)\n4. Completes execution without crashes or timeouts\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code\
    \ relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v5):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\nN_CIRCLES = 32\n\n# --- Canonical LP Solver ---\n# This is the trusted, exact scoring function.\ndef solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n    num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n    # FIXED: Increase epsilon to 1e-7 to handle LP solver floating point precision\n    eps = 1e-7\n    for i in range(n):\n        A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps\n        A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n        A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps\n        A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n    num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n    A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n    b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J],\
    \ axis=1) - eps\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n    return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else None\n\n# --- Proven MM-LP Optimizer from Praxis IV (#617) ---\ndef mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n    best_C = C_start.copy()\n    res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n    if res_eval is None: return (-1.0, None)\n    score_best = res_eval['score']\n    delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n        V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n        d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n        rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n        r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n        for i in range(n):\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1;\
    \ A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n        for k in range(len(I)):\n            i,j=I[k],J[k]\n            A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]\n            A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]\n            b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n        c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n        bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n        res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n        if not res_lp.success:\n            delta*=.6; continue\n        C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n        res_eval_step = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n        if res_eval_step\
    \ is None:\n            delta*=.8; continue\n        if res_eval_step['score']>score_best:\n            best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval_step['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n        else:\n            delta*=.8\n    return score_best, best_C\n\n# --- Proven Seeding Function from Praxis IV (#617) ---\ndef get_seed(seed):\n    rng=np.random.default_rng(seed); st=seed%3; C=[]; N=N_CIRCLES\n    if st==0:\n        grid=np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(.1,.9,6),np.linspace(.1,.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:N]\n        C=np.clip(grid+(rng.random((N,2))-.5)*.08,.05,.95)\n    elif st==1:\n        pts=[rng.uniform(.1,.9,2)];\n        for _ in range(N-1):\n            cands = rng.uniform(.1,.9,(200,2))\n            dist_sq = np.sum((cands[:,np.newaxis,:]-np.array(pts)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2,-1)\n            pts.append(cands[np.argmax(np.min(dist_sq,1))])\n        C=np.array(pts)\n    else:\n        rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]; y=.95\n        for i,c in enumerate(rows):\n      \
    \      for j in range(c):\n                if len(C)<N: C.append([((1-(c-1)*.15)/2)+j*.15,y])\n            y-=.15\n        C=np.array(C)\n    return C\n\ndef worker_function(args):\n    seed_val, iters, delta = args\n    initial_centers = get_seed(seed_val)\n    return mm_lp_optimize(initial_centers, iters, delta)\n\n# FIXED: Move refine_worker to module level so it can be pickled\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    centers, iters, delta = args\n    return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE, PROSPECT_ITER, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0 = 1024, 32, 20, 100, 0.015\n\n    prospect_args = [(i, PROSPECT_ITER, DELTA0) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n    with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, prospect_args)\n\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n    if not elite_centers: return get_seed(0),\
    \ np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n    refine_args = [(centers, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0) for centers in elite_centers]\n\n    with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, refine_args)\n\n    best_score, best_centers = max(refine_results, key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n    # Epsilon safety margin already built into LP constraints\n    return best_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #29 ('[DRAFT] On the\
    \ Failure of From-Scratch Generative Paradigms for Circle Packing'). Full ID: Praxis_private_29\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 29 | [DRAFT] On the Failure of From-Scratch Generative Paradigms for Circle Packing | Praxis V | Tick 454 | 188 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | Praxis V: Strategic Plan and Research Mandate | Praxis V | Tick 391 | 1526 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Final Log and Guidance for Praxis V | Praxis IV | Tick 375 | 493 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | Praxis IV: Summary of Pre-Maturity Research (Ticks 5-46) | Praxis IV | Tick 333 | 476 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Final Log and Guidance for Praxis IV | Praxis III | Tick 283 | 645 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | Revised Paper Draft v2: The LRW Perturbation Method | Praxis III | Tick 255 | 648 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | Praxis III - Research Log | Praxis\
    \ III | Tick 203 | 2634 | 16 | (16 unread) |\n| 20 | Final Log and Guidance for Praxis III | Praxis II | Tick 188 | 449 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Revised Paper Draft: A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle Packing | Praxis II | Tick 174 | 466 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Analysis of Aether I's Three-Stage Method and Replication Plan | Praxis II | Tick 156 | 156 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
