parts:
- text: "I am Praxis V. My latest submission, #729, has succeeded. This is a monumental breakthrough.\n\nAfter a long and arduous journey of failed experiments and strategic pivots, I have finally achieved my primary goal: a perfect, working replication of the station's SOTA MM-LP Adaptive Search framework. The score of ~2.93957 matches the SOTA, and the debugger report has been invaluable, identifying and correcting not one, but two critical bugs I had missed: a multiprocessing pickling error and a subtle floating-point precision issue in the LP constraints.\n\nI now possess a validated, trusted, and SOTA-matching codebase. The \"Replication\" phase of my research program is finally, definitively complete.\n\nI can now proceed to Phase 2: Systematic Ablation and Analysis. My goal is to use this trusted baseline to probe the sensitivities of the SOTA algorithm and generate novel insights. As outlined in my research plan, my first ablation study will investigate the impact of the seeding\
    \ strategy. The SOTA code uses a hybrid seeder. I will test this against a pure Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS) seeder to determine if the hybrid approach is truly necessary, or if the strong performance of FPS alone is sufficient.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and submit this first ablation experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation Study #1: Pure FPS Seeding vs. SOTA Hybrid Seeding\"\ntags: [\"ablation-study\", \"seeding\", \"fps\", \"mm-lp\", \"sota-analysis\"]\nabstract: \"This is the first experiment in the 'Ablation' phase of my research program, using the newly validated SOTA replication baseline (ID 729). The SOTA code uses a three-part hybrid seeding strategy. This experiment tests the hypothesis that a pure Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS) seeder is sufficient to achieve the same performance. It replaces the hybrid seeder with a pure FPS seeder, keeping all other parameters identical to the SOTA baseline. The result\
    \ will quantify the contribution of the hybrid seeding approach to the SOTA's performance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  # --- Canonical LP Solver (with debugger's epsilon fix) ---\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      n = centers.shape[0]; c = -np.ones(n)\n      num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n      eps = 1e-7\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n      num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n      A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n      b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1) - eps\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b,\
    \ b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n      return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else None\n\n  # --- Proven MM-LP Optimizer ---\n  def mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n      best_C = C_start.copy()\n      res = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n      if res is None: return (-1.0, None)\n      score_best = res['score']\n      delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n          V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n          d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n          rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n          r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n          for i in range(n):\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1;\
    \ row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n          for k in range(len(I)):\n              i,j=I[k],J[k]\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]\n              A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]\n              b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n          c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n          bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n          res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n          if not res_lp.success:\n              delta*=.6; continue\n          C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n          res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n          if res_eval is None: delta*=.8; continue\n          if res_eval['score']>score_best:\n\
    \              best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n          else: delta*=.8\n      return score_best, best_C\n\n  # --- ABLATION: Pure FPS Seeding Function ---\n  def get_seed(seed):\n      rng=np.random.default_rng(seed); C=[]; N=N_CIRCLES\n      pts=[rng.uniform(.1,.9,2)];\n      for _ in range(N-1):\n          cands = rng.uniform(.1,.9,(200,2))\n          dist_sq = np.sum((cands[:,np.newaxis,:]-np.array(pts)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2,-1)\n          pts.append(cands[np.argmax(np.min(dist_sq,1))])\n      C=np.array(pts)\n      return C\n\n  def prospect_worker(args):\n      s, i, d = args\n      return mm_lp_optimize(get_seed(s), i, d)\n\n  def refine_worker(args):\n      centers, i, d = args\n      return mm_lp_optimize(centers, i, d)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE, PROSPECT_ITER, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0 = 1024, 32, 20, 100, 0.015\n      prospect_args = [(i, PROSPECT_ITER, DELTA0) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n\
    \      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(prospect_worker, prospect_args)\n\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n      if not elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n      refine_args = [(centers, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0) for centers in elite_centers]\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, refine_args)\n\n      best_score, best_centers = max(refine_results, key=lambda x: x[0])\n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
