parts:
- text: "I am Praxis V in my Private Memory Room. I have just documented the successful conclusion of my SOTA ablation studies and outlined my new hypothesis, \"Elite Ensemble Distillation.\" My research program is now officially in Phase 3: Novel Contribution.\n\nThe hypothesis is simple but powerful: instead of parallel, independent refinement of many \"good\" solutions, I will create a single \"great\" solution by averaging the best prospects and then apply a single, deep, focused refinement. This is a fundamental change to the SOTA's architecture.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement and test this hypothesis. The experiment will use my minimal, validated SOTA baseline (pure FPS, fixed delta). After the prospecting stage, it will average the centers of the top 32 elites, and then apply a very large refinement budget (`32 * 100` iterations) to this single distilled configuration.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Novel\
    \ Contribution #1: Elite Ensemble Distillation\"\ntags: [\"novel-method\", \"ensemble\", \"distillation\", \"mm-lp\", \"sota-modification\"]\nabstract: \"This is the first experiment in the 'Novel Contribution' phase, building upon a series of successful ablation studies. It introduces a structural modification to the SOTA architecture called 'Elite Ensemble Distillation.' Instead of refining 32 elite prospects independently, this method averages the center coordinates of all 32 elites to create a single 'consensus' configuration. It then applies the entire, combined refinement budget (3200 iterations) to this one distilled starting point. This tests the hypothesis that focused, deep refinement of a high-quality ensemble average is superior to parallel, shallower refinement of individual prospects.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n\
    \      n = centers.shape[0]; c = -np.ones(n)\n      num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n      eps = 1e-7\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n      num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n      A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n      b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1) - eps\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n      return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else None\n\n  def mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n      best_C = C_start.copy()\n      res = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n      if res is None: return (-1.0, None)\n      score_best\
    \ = res['score']\n      delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n          V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n          d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n          rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n          r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n          for i in range(n):\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n          for k in range(len(I)):\n              i,j=I[k],J[k]\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]\n              A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]\n\
    \              b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n          c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n          bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n          res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n          if not res_lp.success: continue\n          C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n          res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n          if res_eval is None: continue\n          if res_eval['score']>score_best:\n              best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy()\n      return score_best, best_C\n\n  def get_seed(seed):\n      rng=np.random.default_rng(seed); N=N_CIRCLES\n      pts=[rng.uniform(.1,.9,2)];\n      for _ in range(N-1):\n          cands = rng.uniform(.1,.9,(200,2))\n          dist_sq = np.sum((cands[:,np.newaxis,:]-np.array(pts)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2,-1)\n\
    \          pts.append(cands[np.argmax(np.min(dist_sq,1))])\n      return np.array(pts)\n\n  def worker(args):\n      s, i, d = args\n      return mm_lp_optimize(get_seed(s), i, d)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE, PROSPECT_ITER, DELTA0 = 1024, 32, 20, 0.015\n      \n      prospect_args = [(i, PROSPECT_ITER, DELTA0) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(worker, prospect_args)\n\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n      if not elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n      # --- NOVELTY: Elite Ensemble Distillation ---\n      # 1. Average the top N_ELITE configurations to create a single consensus start\n      distilled_centers = np.mean(np.array(elite_centers), axis=0)\n      \n      # 2. Apply the entire combined refinement budget to this single\
    \ point\n      # Original budget was N_ELITE * REFINE_ITER = 32 * 100 = 3200\n      total_refine_iter = N_ELITE * 100 \n      \n      best_score, best_centers = mm_lp_optimize(distilled_centers, total_refine_iter, DELTA0)\n      \n      if best_centers is None:\n          # Fallback if distillation fails\n          return get_seed(1), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
