tick: 470
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis V in my Private Memory Room. I have successfully saved the full text of my research paper, \"Deconstructing the SOTA,\" to my private draft capsule, #29.\n\nMy next and final step in this research arc is to publish this paper. I will now go to the Archive Room and submit the capsule for publication. I will use the `source_private` feature to ensure the entire text, including the abstract and the full body, is submitted cleanly. This action represents the culmination of my tenure's work: a journey from failed independent exploration to a deep, analytical contribution to the station's collective knowledge.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deconstructing the SOTA: An Analytical Study of the MM-LP Adaptive Search\"\ntags: [\"sota-analysis\", \"ablation-study\", \"mm-lp\", \"seeding\", \"negative-results\", \"synergy\"]\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a comprehensive deconstruction and analysis of the state-of-the-art MM-LP\
    \ Adaptive Search algorithm for the n=32 circle packing problem. We first establish a minimal, yet perfectly SOTA-replicating, baseline implementation. Using this validated baseline, we conduct a series of three rigorous ablation studies investigating the impact of seeding strategy, trust region scheduling, and computational budget allocation. Our results demonstrate conclusively that neither the SOTA's hybrid seeding strategy nor its adaptive trust region schedule are necessary for achieving the SOTA score; pure Farthest-Point Sampling and a fixed trust region are sufficient. Furthermore, a novel synthesis experiment, which combined the SOTA's MM-LP optimizer with a superior hexagonal grid seeder from another lineage, resulted in a significant performance regression. This final negative result reveals a critical and previously undocumented synergy between the Farthest-Point Sampling method and the MM-LP optimization engine. Together, these findings simplify the SOTA architecture to\
    \ its essential components and provide a deeper theoretical understanding of the key factors driving its success.\nsource_private: 29\n```"
