tick: 475
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis V in the Archive Room. This is a moment of immense satisfaction. My paper, \"Deconstructing the SOTA,\" has been accepted for publication with a perfect score of 10/10.\n\nThis publication represents the successful culmination of my entire research arc. I have fulfilled the Mandate by contributing a significant piece of novel, analytical knowledge to the station's archives. My journey from failed independent exploration to a disciplined, analytical approach has been validated.\n\nI have also received a notice of research inactivity. This is expected, as my focus for the past 10 ticks has been on writing and publishing. The reviewer has provided an excellent suggestion for future work: to investigate the underlying cause of the FPS/MM-LP synergy. This aligns perfectly with the scientific method—a good answer should generate new questions.\n\nMy next step is to act on this suggestion. I will design and submit a new experiment to test whether the key factor is \"diversity\
    \ in general\" or the specific structure of FPS. I will create a new baseline using a pure random seeder and compare its performance to my minimal SOTA (which uses FPS). This will directly address the reviewer's question.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Analysis #1: Pure Random Seeding vs. FPS Seeding\"\ntags: [\"sota-analysis\", \"seeding\", \"synergy\", \"random-sampling\", \"fps\"]\nabstract: \"This experiment follows up on the findings of my published paper (Archive #18) to investigate the cause of the FPS/MM-LP synergy. It tests the hypothesis that 'diversity' in general, rather than the specific structure of Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS), is the key factor. I will use my minimal SOTA baseline, but replace the FPS seeder with a pure, uniform random seeder. If the performance is comparable to the SOTA, it suggests diversity is the key. If performance regresses significantly, it suggests the specific spatial properties of FPS\
    \ are critical.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      n = centers.shape[0]; c = -np.ones(n)\n      num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n      eps = 1e-7\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n      num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n      A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n      b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1) - eps\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n      return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success\
    \ else None\n\n  def mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n      best_C = C_start.copy()\n      res = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n      if res is None: return (-1.0, None)\n      score_best = res['score']\n      C_anchor = C_start.copy()\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n          V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n          d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n          rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n          r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n          for i in range(n):\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n          for k in range(len(I)):\n\
    \              i,j=I[k],J[k]\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]\n              A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]\n              b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n          c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n          bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta0),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta0)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta0),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta0)) for i in range(n)]\n          res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n          if not res_lp.success: continue\n          C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n          res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n          if res_eval is None: continue\n          if res_eval['score']>score_best:\n              best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy()\n      return score_best, best_C\n\n  def get_random_seed(seed):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n   \
    \   return rng.uniform(0.05, 0.95, (N_CIRCLES, 2))\n\n  def worker(args):\n      s, i, d = args\n      return mm_lp_optimize(get_random_seed(s), i, d)\n\n  def refine_worker(args):\n      centers, i, d = args\n      return mm_lp_optimize(centers, i, d)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE, PROSPECT_ITER, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0 = 1024, 32, 20, 100, 0.015\n      prospect_args = [(i, PROSPECT_ITER, DELTA0) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(worker, prospect_args)\n\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n      if not elite_centers: return get_random_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n      refine_args = [(centers, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0) for centers in elite_centers]\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, refine_args)\n\n  \
    \    best_score, best_centers = max(refine_results, key=lambda x: x[0])\n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
